+# Original C++ SDK catalog observations outside selected compiler roots
+
+The complete original `tools/ros_distro/common.catalog` contract records literal symlinks without following directory links. A directory target must remain within the explicit whole-root set. An external **regular file** target is separately opened and pinned in that exact symlink row. An unused regular target observation is not automatically a selected compiler input or authority to use its parent directory.
+
+The independently completed C++ abort object's original 58 catalogs include such observations. Root's actual bounded metadata observation scanned 178188 original rows and found 358 distinct external regular target names, all preserved with the explicit historical host-device transition 66307 to 66312. This observation does not make the files compiler inputs and does not justify selecting `/usr`, `/etc`, `/opt` or any arbitrary ancestor. It is not official ROS, Guest or Runtime acceptance. The original Source49 reports and frozen source remain unchanged.
+
+The narrow successor keeps ordinary `Evidence.pin` unchanged. The consumed compiler, full-MD headers, object/depfile/log products, official LLVM source/lock files and complete original source must still satisfy the existing selected whole-root/source boundary. There is no fallback from that accessor into the catalog-only ledger, and the ledger never populates `Evidence.cache`, `Frame.inputs`, `Frame.roots` or `Frame.pins`.
+
+Only the complete `catalog_pair` stream can invoke `_observe_catalog_target`. It retains the original/current catalog full pins and the exact original/current literal source rows. Both complete catalog file descriptors and their names are bracketed and fully hashed by the existing comparison. Row order, relative names, kind, source literal target/resolution, inode, timestamps, size and SHA remain exact. An external target's distinct device is accepted only under the selected **source catalog root's explicit restart transition**; it grants no authority over the target's directory. Both old and new target full7 values remain separately recorded.
+
+Each newly observed target is reopened through the existing restart helper: every ancestor uses held directory descriptors and `O_NOFOLLOW`, the final descriptor uses `O_NOFOLLOW|O_NONBLOCK`, only ordinary regular files are accepted, and the full byte stream, stable before/after fstat and named-entry identity must agree. A device change uses the strict persistent-file bridge, permitting only the explicit device field difference while preserving path, inode, mtime, ctime, size and SHA. The actual current pin must equal the current Frame catalog's `target_file`. Same-device observations require the two exact full pins and an independent current full read. The original source symlink itself is separately rechecked before and after observation, including its literal text, resolved target and physical identity. Neither a directory, FIFO, source-alias replacement nor changed target bytes can use this role.
+
+The separate `whole_catalog_observed_external_regular_targets` sidecar ledger has at most 4096 names and 512 MiB per target. Repeated identical names are recorded once with every exact source-row/catalog witness. This is finite memoization of the original selected catalog rows, not a directory scan for permission or a recursive report projection. Every admitted external file and every source alias is reopened after the ordinary full-MD and official-source checks, before qualification sidecar publication.
+
+The actual Legacy producer's normal `Frame.finish` remains mandatory after compilation. It repeats all complete current input catalogs and compares their original `target_file` rows, independently covering these same observations after the actor cleanup. A metadata sidecar is not a terminal Guest build success. Old raw statuses and historical cgroup facts are never rewritten, and a same numeric filesystem device does not establish process or cgroup continuity.
+
+`test_cpp_catalog_observations.py` provides fourteen authored real-filesystem/DATA cases through `cases(helper, restart, *, temporary_parent, guard)`. Root must supply both complete-manifest-bound helpers, an owned temporary directory parent and the actual current64 guard. The tests import no project module, create no compiler/ROS/Runtime actor and do not qualify synthetic catalogs as authentic SDK receipts. The author did not import or execute the candidate or tests. The existing eleven independent-CPP policy cases remain unchanged.
+
+The change intentionally retains the native producer's current-source equality rule. Root must select a newly completed native report from the actual new complete source freeze before executing the later Guest producer; no old Source49 report is relabelled as a new compilation.
